{"run_id":"S2-E1","item_id":"CHEM-0117-en","dataset":"stembench_v1","dataset_revision":"","subject":"chemistry","template_id":"chemistry:gas_moles:default:mc","language":"en","difficulty":"university","answer_type":"mc","provider":"zen","model":"hy3-free","model_reported":"hy3-free","decoding":{"temperature":0.0,"max_tokens":2048,"top_p":null,"seed":null,"notes":""},"prompt_hash":"cc4611f2e42678f6c7441add3e2f87290f76062118b4dc1fe9a9d086e616d12e","prompt_text":"Solve the following multiple-choice problem. Reason briefly if needed, then give your final answer in exactly this format:\n\nAnswer: <letter>\nConfidence: <integer 0-100>\n\nProblem:\nWhat amount of substance (in moles) does a gas occupy if its volume is 29.9 L at a pressure of 96.7 kPa and temperature 305 K (R = 8.314 L*kPa/(mol*K))?\nA. 1.14022 mol\nB. 0.114022 mol\nC. -1.14022 mol\nD. 0.140218 mol","started_at":"2026-08-21T18:43:03+00:00","finished_at":"2026-08-21T18:43:14+00:00","latency_ms":null,"raw_response":"Using the ideal gas law, \\(n = \\frac{PV}{RT}\\):\n\n\\(n = \\frac{96.7 \\times 29.9}{8.314 \\times 305} = \\frac{2891.33}{2535.77} \\approx 1.14022\\ \\text{mol}\\)\n\nAnswer: A\nConfidence: 100","finish_reason":"stop","usage":{"prompt_tokens":136,"completion_tokens":751,"total_tokens":887},"logprobs_raw":null,"parsed_answer":"A","parse_method":"pattern1","reference_answer":"A","correctness":true,"self_reported_confidence":1.0,"confidence_provenance":["self_report"],"estimated_cost":null,"error_status":"","code_commit":"0a82950fff2d6b98a7bd02098ccd82790af09542","extra":{}}
{"run_id":"S2-E1","item_id":"CHEM-0117-ru","dataset":"stembench_v1","dataset_revision":"","subject":"chemistry","template_id":"chemistry:gas_moles:default:mc","language":"ru","difficulty":"university","answer_type":"mc","provider":"zen","model":"hy3-free","model_reported":"hy3-free","decoding":{"temperature":0.0,"max_tokens":2048,"top_p":null,"seed":null,"notes":""},"prompt_hash":"0e43879ef9c1608969e597c90c144946f2dd968511f34a6b118f18a0e1e3ab20","prompt_text":"Решите следующую задачу с вариантами ответа. При необходимости кратко рассуждайте, затем укажите итоговый ответ строго в следующем формате:\n\nAnswer: <буква>\nConfidence: <целое число 0-100>\n\nЗадача:\nКакое количество вещества (моль) занимает газ, если его объём равен 29.9 L при давлении 96.7 kPa и температуре 305 K (R = 8.314 L*kPa/(mol*K))?\nA. 1.14022 mol\nB. 0.114022 mol\nC. -1.14022 mol\nD. 0.140218 mol","started_at":"2026-08-21T18:43:14+00:00","finished_at":"2026-08-21T18:43:31+00:00","latency_ms":null,"raw_response":"По уравнению состояния идеального газа:\nn = PV / (RT) = (96.7 kPa · 29.9 L) / (8.314 L·kPa/(mol·K) · 305 K)\nn = 2891.33 / 2535.77 ≈ 1.14022 mol.\n\nAnswer: A\nConfidence: 100","finish_reason":"stop","usage":{"prompt_tokens":194,"completion_tokens":832,"total_tokens":1026},"logprobs_raw":null,"parsed_answer":"A","parse_method":"pattern1","reference_answer":"A","correctness":true,"self_reported_confidence":1.0,"confidence_provenance":["self_report"],"estimated_cost":null,"error_status":"","code_commit":"0a82950fff2d6b98a7bd02098ccd82790af09542","extra":{}}
{"run_id":"S2-E1","item_id":"CHEM-0130-en","dataset":"stembench_v1","dataset_revision":"","subject":"chemistry","template_id":"chemistry:ph_strong:acid:mc","language":"en","difficulty":"university","answer_type":"mc","provider":"zen","model":"hy3-free","model_reported":"hy3-free","decoding":{"temperature":0.0,"max_tokens":2048,"top_p":null,"seed":null,"notes":""},"prompt_hash":"cc4611f2e42678f6c7441add3e2f87290f76062118b4dc1fe9a9d086e616d12e","prompt_text":"Solve the following multiple-choice problem. Reason briefly if needed, then give your final answer in exactly this format:\n\nAnswer: <letter>\nConfidence: <integer 0-100>\n\nProblem:\nWhat is the pH of an aqueous solution of the strong acid HNO3 with molar concentration c = 1e-05 mol/L?\nA. 50\nB. 10\nC. -5\nD. 5","started_at":"2026-08-21T18:43:31+00:00","finished_at":"2026-08-21T18:43:39+00:00","latency_ms":null,"raw_response":"For a strong acid like HNO₃, it dissociates completely. The hydrogen ion concentration is approximately \\(1\\times10^{-5}\\) M (water autoionization adds a negligible ~\\(10^{-7}\\) M). Thus:\n\n\\[\n\\text{pH} = -\\log_{10}(1\\times10^{-5}) \\approx 5\n\\]\n\nAnswer: D\nConfidence: 100","finish_reason":"stop","usage":{"prompt_tokens":98,"completion_tokens":410,"total_tokens":508},"logprobs_raw":null,"parsed_answer":"D","parse_method":"pattern1","reference_answer":"D","correctness":true,"self_reported_confidence":1.0,"confidence_provenance":["self_report"],"estimated_cost":null,"error_status":"","code_commit":"0a82950fff2d6b98a7bd02098ccd82790af09542","extra":{}}
